  "title": "MCP is Not Secure",
  "summary": "MCP standardizes how AI agents connect to tools and data. What it doesn't do is secure them. The spec addresses authentication plumbing but leaves authorization decisions to implementers. So how do you build with MCP without recreating the mistakes behind 2025's breach timeline? It starts with understanding where the protocol ends and your responsibility begins.",
